(*!
<summary>
Beckhoff EL3403: 3-phase power measurement terminal up to 500 V AC (1 A / 5 A external CT).
</summary>
<description>
Represents phase TxPDOs 0x1A00..0x1A02, terminal Status TxPDO 0x1A03 and selector RxPDOs 0x1600..0x1602.
All status endpoints are required. Phase headers carry sync error/toggle; terminal Status carries missing
zero crossings, phase sequence error and sync error. Evaluate these alongside bus WcState.
Use each input Index acknowledgement to interpret VariantValue; State=OP alone does not validate a measurement.
Link fields individually. Use one owner task and externally synchronize other access; snapshots are not atomic.
When used for I/O, link located fields or their containing buffers to the matching selected PDOs.
The record is not a packed wire buffer; compiler padding is not part of the device specification.
Unlinked/default values do not prove valid I/O. The caller evaluates bus/channel validity before use.
Use one owner task per instance and externally synchronize other access; multi-field snapshots are not atomic.
Copies store data without creating hardware links. Keep borrowed field references valid while consumers are bound.
This passive record performs no validation, synchronization, configuration or protocol advancement.
</description>
*)
TYPE EL3403 :
STRUCT
	L1 : EL3403_CHANNEL;
	L2 : EL3403_CHANNEL;
	L3 : EL3403_CHANNEL;
	//! <summary>TxPDO 0x1A03: missing zero crossings bits 3..5, phase error bit 8 and sync error bit 13.</summary>
	Status AT %I* : WORD;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>
